<title>USA: U.S. Justice Dept. clears Bell Atlantic-Nynex deal.</title>
<headline>U.S. Justice Dept. clears Bell Atlantic-Nynex deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Thursday it approved Bell Atlantic Corp.'s huge merger with Nynex Corp., the last major hurdle facing the $23 billion deal announced a year ago.</p>
<p>The newly created carrier would be the second-largest U.S. telecommunications company, behind only long-distance giant AT&amp;T Corp. The department's antitrust division spent months probing the transaction to determine if it would block competition in the phone business.</p>
</text>
